{"user": "Wait, c8 only flips 1 for me, and it leaves White b6 which flips my whole b2-b5 column. Isn't taking b6 myself better since it denies that AND gains 4?", "user_ts": "2026-08-04T01:38:23.893398+00:00", "assistant": "No \u2014 **play c8**.\n\nYour point is right locally: after **c8**, White can play **b6** and flip **b2\u2013b5**. But that big-looking flip is **not final** and it costs White a move/tempo.\n\nIf you play **b6** first, you deny that column flip, but you hand White the important reply **c8** and lose the endgame timing. In this position the quiet **c8** is the move that wins with best play; **b6** is the tempting \u201cgrab/deny\u201d move that falls short.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-04T01:38:23.893398+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-04T01:38:28.893398+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Common Ground Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line"], "consensus": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line"], "votes": {"Move Verdict": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 3, "Neutral Feedback": 1, "General Principle": 1, "Paraphrase": 1, "Positive Feedback": 1, "Negative Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Move Verdict": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 1.0, "Neutral Feedback": 0.3333333333333333, "General Principle": 0.3333333333333333, "Paraphrase": 0.3333333333333333, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333, "Negative Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Move Verdict", "Local